From: Avocado Linux <info@avocadolinux.org>
Subject: [PATCH] wiringPi: call GetRP1Memory() with no arguments

GetRP1Memory takes no parameters - it fills the file-scope pciemem_RP1
buffer directly - but the one call site passes (pciemem_RP1,
sizeof(pciemem_RP1)). Under C17 the empty parameter list left the
function unprototyped, so the extra arguments were merely ignored; GCC 15
defaults to C23, where () means (void), and the call is an error:

  wiringPi.c:3281:5: error: too many arguments to function 'GetRP1Memory';
  expected 0, have 2

Drop the arguments. Nothing else reads them, and the RP1 path is
Raspberry Pi 5-only code that never runs on this board anyway.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor fork, rubikpi-ai/WiringRP]
---
--- a/wiringPi/wiringPi.c
+++ b/wiringPi/wiringPi.c
@@ -3278,7 +3278,7 @@
 
   piBoard();
   if (PI_MODEL_5 == RaspberryPiModel) {
-    GetRP1Memory(pciemem_RP1, sizeof(pciemem_RP1));
+    GetRP1Memory();
     gpiomemGlobal = pciemem_RP1;
     MMAP_size = pciemem_RP1_Size;
     BaseAddr  = 0x00000000;
